{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787679653455059002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"soldierly-whacky-merlin","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"3dad22d3f7940d063bf8d1b346c54f5288249eeefecbb9764c0983635b9c57e4","event_uuid":"cad3ebd0-869c-4fbb-97d9-263150e738b5","position":{"commit_sha":"257732f62ffa7ffc495dc98dd1043ccb24344818","position":"1787679545739783001-cad3ebd0-869c-4fbb-97d9-263150e738b5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"49a48d6614a052e9ec720cced036b89c546d49042bcc43f51dd43e9535e50b3b","event_uuid":"d60b4d5b-d1be-4a46-b5c1-a37bdfa64c21","position":{"commit_sha":"5575635ecdee6325bb554671ca00976d77219ce6","position":"1787679600080734001-d60b4d5b-d1be-4a46-b5c1-a37bdfa64c21"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8358d9e207bf2ab6a24c1d03a4c0d23256a4e606eb7765c84ad2c7bd8427c059","event_uuid":"a15a2237-c331-4f14-a591-62ea80f13a9f","position":{"commit_sha":"9ad0c44d7e09c5ca1c2cd5f49866960c06cd4bc4","position":"1787679625794704001-a15a2237-c331-4f14-a591-62ea80f13a9f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1abec744cfc80d2cec1837aa6a55b2aba7b076a4521af5b802905a5fc9488efb","event_uuid":"3384b82d-9956-4ccf-a515-d8f5e82dac6d","position":{"commit_sha":"fb2adc45846f52734e8a5914e574e6a4681d6446","position":"1787679653455059001-3384b82d-9956-4ccf-a515-d8f5e82dac6d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787679545739783001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3384b82d-9956-4ccf-a515-d8f5e82dac6d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"807d-3357-726e-4faa"}],"description":"## Context\n\nThe code-review documentation specialist declares `execution_mode: single_turn`, while its routing entry declares `exec: 1-TURN`. The runner therefore withholds repository tools. Its rubric also requires every contradiction to appear entirely inside the diff. This prevents grounded detection when a changed public contract requires an update to maintained documentation. The rubric does not apply the documentation roles and correction rules in `docs/documentation-policy.md`.\n\nThe approved design upgrades this specialist to the same agentic execution model used by other repository-grounded code-review criteria. It preserves advisory treatment and rejects stylistic enforcement.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Change the prompt execution mode to `agentic` and the routing execution mode to `AGENT`. Regenerate the derived reviewer index from prompt front matter.\n- Revise the documentation rubric to require read-only repository navigation before reporting missing updates or role violations.\n- Replace the diff-only contradiction rule with a two-source rule. Every finding must cite a changed `path:line` and a second repository source that proves inaccuracy, required ownership, or a bounded omission.\n- Add a missing-update check for changed user, operator, API, CLI, configuration, and shipped-help contracts. Permit absence findings only when repository evidence establishes the canonical documentation location and a bounded search confirms the omission. A repository-wide search with no match is insufficient.\n- Add a documentation-role check based on `docs/documentation-policy.md` and `docs/generated-artifacts.md`. Apply it to changed maintained documentation, shipped help, comments, ADRs, and generated artifacts. Require policy citations and abstention when audience, role, or ownership is ambiguous.\n- Preserve the existing automatic file globs, advisory posture, blocking setting, impact-aware nit suppression, and independent Pass 2 verification. Do not add punctuation, character, vocabulary, diction, tone, wrapping, or subjective concision enforcement.\n- Add balanced prompt regression cases and contract tests for agentic execution, grounded missing-update findings, role violations, protected evidence, and false-positive abstention.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The documentation overlay front matter, routing entry, and generated reviewer index agree that the overlay uses agentic execution with repository tools.\n- [ ] The rubric requires every finding to contain a changed-text anchor and repository-backed evidence.\n- [ ] Missing-update findings require a repository-proven documentation obligation and a bounded search. Generic absence speculation remains prohibited.\n- [ ] Documentation-role findings apply the explicit role and correction rules in `docs/documentation-policy.md` and generated ownership in `docs/generated-artifacts.md`. Ambiguous roles produce no finding.\n- [ ] Protected evidence, quotations, historical ticket events, ADR decision substance, and writing-style preferences remain outside the criterion.\n- [ ] Existing routing globs, advisory posture, blocking setting, nit suppression, and Pass 2 verification remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Balanced regression coverage includes proven missing updates and role violations, plus internal-only changes, ambiguous ownership, and unrelated unchanged documentation that must produce no finding.\n- [ ] Focused prompt, routing, index, and regression tests pass, followed by repository lint and type checks.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-docs.md","reason":"Upgrade the documentation rubric to agentic repository-grounded evaluation."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json","reason":"Declare AGENT execution while preserving routing posture and globs."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json","reason":"Regenerate the derived prompt catalog after the execution-mode change."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-docs.eval.yaml","reason":"Add balanced prompt regression cases for omissions, roles, and abstention."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_docs_overlay.py","reason":"Pin agentic execution and the evidence and role contracts."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_nit_suppression.py","reason":"Retire the obsolete diff-only rubric assertions while preserving nit behavior tests."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_evals.py","reason":"Add the documentation specification to standing offline eval validation."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["code-review","documentation","llm"],"ticket_id":"b126-b52c-f2bc-49bb","ticket_type":"task","title":"Make the code-review documentation overlay agentic","verify_commands":[{"command":".venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_code_review_docs_overlay.py tests/unit/test_code_review_ws2.py tests/unit/test_generated_surface_markers.py","dd_id":"DD1","dd_text":"Agentic prompt, routing, and generated index stay aligned."},{"command":".venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_code_review_evals.py tests/unit/test_code_review_nit_suppression.py","dd_id":"DD2","dd_text":"Documentation prompt regressions include fire and no-fire cases and remain strict-clean."},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck","dd_id":"DD3","dd_text":"Changed Python tests, JSON routing, generated metadata, and prompt text satisfy repository quality gates."}]},"source_event_uuids":["cad3ebd0-869c-4fbb-97d9-263150e738b5","d60b4d5b-d1be-4a46-b5c1-a37bdfa64c21","a15a2237-c331-4f14-a591-62ea80f13a9f","3384b82d-9956-4ccf-a515-d8f5e82dac6d"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787679653455059002,"uuid":"9eabaf28-ab6f-470c-815f-9dba4142811f"}